From 15b4344a8f29a52532f9ba8b25da6d1180be73b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:00:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(multiaxis): Rotary Parallel leaves the end face of a held
 end

Rotary Parallel ran its raster over the whole model and did not know the
stock. On a bar held in a chuck, the pass down the chuck-side end face was
a slot one tool wide from the skin to the axis: it parted the bar.

The kind now reads the setup stock. Where the stock goes on past an end of
the model by more than one tool diameter, the centre of the ball does not
go past that end plane: the end face is left, the turned surface is
finished to its end, and a note names the end. A sloped entry does not
start past a held end. A free end, and a facing allowance of one tool
diameter or less, are cut as before.

The #1904 example project and program are generated again, and the guide
pages and pictures follow the new program.

Fixes #2343

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
